  <iati-identifier>GB-CHC-202918-DRCC67</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-202918" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam GB</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving Integrated WASH,EFSL and Protection for conflict affected comminuties</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve, by October 2025,  the socio -sanitary conditions of the populations affected by the crisis by ensuring:  - Access to potable water in Internally Displaced Person (IDP) sites, host communities and health centres;  - Access to adequate, dignified and hygienic sanitation facilities and,  - ensuring a systematic approach to encourage the widespread adoption of safe hygiene practices to keep people and their environment clean through the promotion of hygiene knowledge and practices and community engagement;  - responding to emergency food needs, the acquisition of essential household items, and primary health care coverage by organizing &quot;multi -purpose cash distributions&quot; (food, essential household items, and health);  - Contributing to the adoption of better community protection practices, reducing the risk of violence and abuse, particularly for women, girls, and disproportionately affected groups in the intervention area. This project will be implemented directly in Ituri and Tanganyika Provinces with the collaboration of the central office of the health zone and the local communities. An estimated number of 13333 Households have been targeted for this project. The project targets internally displaced persons (19%), returnees (49%) and residents of host communities (32%), reaching a total of 80,000 persons (without double counting)</narrative>
  </description>
